H8400.definition:
from H1101 (בָּלַל) in the original sense of flowing;
a cataract (in the eye)
KJV: blemish.

H8401.definition:
probably from H1129 (בָּנָה);
properly, material, i.e. (specifically) refuse haum or stalks of grain (as chopped in threshing and used for fodder)
KJV: chaff, straw, stubble.

H8402.definition:
from H8401 (תֶּבֶן); strawy;
Tibni, an Israelite
KJV: Tibni.

H8403.definition:
from H1129 (בָּנָה);
structure; by implication, a model, resemblance
KJV: figure, form, likeness, pattern, similitude.

H8404.definition:
from H1197 (בָּעַר); burning;
Taberah, a place in the Desert
KJV: Taberah.

H8405.definition:
from the same as H948 (בּוּץ); whiteness;
Tebets, a place in Palestine
KJV: Thebez.

H8406.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7665 (שָׁבַר);
to be fragile (figuratively)
KJV: broken.

H8407.definition:
or תִּגְלַת פְּלֶסֶר; or תִּלְגַּת פִּלְנְאֶסֶר or תִּלְגַּת פִּלְנֶסֶר; of foreign derivation;
Tiglath-Pileser or Tilgath-pilneser, an Assyryrian king
KJV: Tiglath-pileser, Tilgath-pilneser.

H8408.definition:
from H1580 (גָּמַל);
a bestowment
KJV: benefit.

H8409.definition:
from H1624 (גָּרָה);
strife, i.e. infliction
KJV: blow.

H8410.definition:
apparently from H1725 (דָּהַר);
enduring; a species of hard-wood or lasting tree (perhaps oak)
KJV: pine (tree).

H8411.definition:
(Aramaic) from H1753 (דּוּר) in the original sense of enduring;
permanence, i.e. (adverb) constantly
KJV: continually.

H8412.definition:
or תַּמֹּר; (1 Kings 9:18), apparently from H8558 (תָּמָר); palm-city;
Tadmor, a place near Palestine
KJV: Tadmor.

H8413.definition:
perhaps from H1763 (דְּחַל); fearfulness;
Tidal, a Canaanite
KJV: Tidal.

H8414.definition:
from an unused root meaning to lie waste;
a desolation (of surface), i.e. desert; figuratively, a worthless thing; adverbially, in vain
KJV: confusion, empty place, without form, nothing, (thing of) nought, vain, vanity, waste, wilderness.

H8415.definition:
or תְּהֹם; (usually feminine) from H1949 (הוּם);
an abyss (as a surging mass of water), especially the deep (the main sea or the subterranean watersupply)
KJV: deep (place), depth.

H8416.definition:
from H1984 (הָלַל);
laudation; specifically (concretely) a hymn
KJV: praise.

H8417.definition:
feminine of an unused noun (apparently from H1984 (הָלַל)) meaning bluster;
braggadocio, i.e. (by implication) fatuity
KJV: folly.

H8418.definition:
from H1980 (הָלַךְ);
a procession
KJV: [idiom] went.

H8419.definition:
from H2015 (הָפַךְ);
a perversity or fraud
KJV: (very) froward(-ness, thing), perverse thing.

H8420.definition:
from H8427 (תָּוָה);
a mark; by implication, a signature
KJV: desire, mark.

H8421.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7725 (שׁוּב), to come back;
specifically (transitive and ellip.) to reply
KJV: answer, restore, return (an answer).

H8422.definition:
or תֻּבַל; probably of foreign derivation;
Tubal, a postdiluvian patriarch and his posterity
KJV: Tubal.

H8423.definition:
apparently from H2986 (יָבַל) (compare H2981 (יְבוּל)) and H7014 (קַיִן); offspring of Cain;
Tubal-Kajin, an antidiluvian patriarch
KJV: Tubal-cain.

H8424.definition:
from H3013 (יָגָה);
depression (of spirits); concretely a grief
KJV: heaviness, sorrow.

H8425.definition:
or תֹּגַרְמָה; probably of foreign derivation;
Togarmah, a son of Gomer and his posterity
KJV: Togarmah.

H8426.definition:
from H3034 (יָדָה);
properly, an extension of the hand, i.e. (by implication) avowal, or (usually) adoration; specifically, a choir of worshippers
KJV: confession, (sacrifice of) praise, thanks(-giving, offering).

H8427.definition:
a primitive root;
to mark out, i.e. (primitive) scratch or (definite) imprint
KJV: scrabble, set (a mark).

H8428.definition:
a primitive root (or perhaps identical with H8427 (תָּוָה) through a similar idea from scraping to pieces);
to grieve
KJV: limit (by confusion with H8427 (תָּוָה)).

H8429.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8539 (תָּמַהּ) or perhaps to H7582 (שָׁאָה) through the idea of sweeping to ruin (compare H8428 (תָּוָה));
to amaze, i.e. (reflex. by implication) take alarm
KJV: be astonied.

H8430.definition:
from an unused root meaning to depress; humble;
Toach, an Israelite
KJV: Toah.

H8432.definition:
from an unused root meaning to sever;
a bisection, i.e. (by implication) the centre
KJV: among(-st), [idiom] between, half, [idiom] (there-, where-), in(-to), middle, mid(-night), midst (among), [idiom] out (of), [idiom] through, [idiom] with(-in).

H8433.definition:
and תּוֹכַחַת; from H3198 (יָכַח);
chastisement; figuratively (by words) correction, refutation, proof (even in defence)
KJV: argument, [idiom] chastened, correction, reasoning, rebuke, reproof, [idiom] be (often) reproved.

H8434.definition:
from H3205 (יָלַד); posterity;
Tolad, a place in Palestine
KJV: Tolad. Compare H513 (אֶלְתּוֹלַד).

H8435.definition:
or תֹּלְדָה; from H3205 (יָלַד);
(plural only) descent, i.e. family; (figuratively) history
KJV: birth, generations.

H8436.definition:
from H8524 (תָּלַל); suspension;
Tulon, an Israelite
KJV: Tilon (from the margin).

H8437.definition:
from H3213 (יָלַל);
causing to howl, i.e. an oppressor
KJV: that wasted.

H8439.definition:
the same as H8438 (תּוֹלָע); worm;
Tola, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Tola.

H8440.definition:
patronymically from H8439 (תּוֹלָע);
a Tolaite (collectively) or descendants of Tola
KJV: Tolaites.

H8441.definition:
or תֹּעֵבַה; feminine active participle of H8581 (תַּעָב);
properly, something disgusting (morally), i.e. (as noun) an abhorrence; especially idolatry or (concretely) an idol
KJV: abominable (custom, thing), abomination.

H8442.definition:
feminine active participle of H8582 (תָּעָה);
mistake, i.e. (morally) impiety, or (political) injury
KJV: error, hinder.

H8443.definition:
from H3286 (יָעַף);
(only in plural collective) weariness, i.e. (by implication) toil (treasure so obtained) or speed
KJV: plenty, strength.

H8444.definition:
or תֹּצָאָה; from H3318 (יָצָא);
(only in plural collective) exit, i.e. (geographical) boundary, or (figuratively) deliverance, (actively) source
KJV: border(-s), going(-s) forth (out), issues, outgoings.

H8445.definition:
from the same as H3349 (יִקָּהָה); obedience;
Tokahath, an Israelite
KJV: Tikvath (by correction for H8616 (תִּקְוָה)).

H8446.definition:
a primitive root;
to meander (causatively, guide) about, especially fortrade or reconnoitring
KJV: chap(-man), sent to descry, be excellent, merchant(-man), search (out), seek, (e-) spy (out).

H8447.definition:
or תֹּר; from H8446 (תּוּר);
a succession, i.e. a string or (abstractly) order
KJV: border, row, turn.

H8448.definition:
probably the same as H8447 (תּוֹר);
a manner (as a sort of turn)
KJV: estate.

H8449.definition:
or תֹּר; probably the same as H8447 (תּוֹר);
a ring-dove, often (figuratively) as a term of endearment
KJV: (turtle) dove.

H8450.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding (by permutation) to H7794 (שׁוֹר);
a bull
KJV: bullock, ox.

H8451.definition:
or תֹּרָה; from H3384 (יָרָה);
a precept or statute, especially the Decalogue or Pentateuch
KJV: law.

H8452.definition:
probably feminine of H8448 (תּוֹר);
a custom
KJV: manner.

H8454.definition:
or תֻּשִׁיָּה; from an unused root probably meaning to substantiate;
support or (by implication) ability, i.e. (direct) help, (in purpose) an undertaking, (intellectual) understanding
KJV: enterprise, that which (thing as it) is, substance, (sound) wisdom, working.

H8455.definition:
from an unused root meaning to smite;
a club
KJV: darts.

H8456.definition:
a primitive root;
to lop off
KJV: cut down.

H8457.definition:
or תַּזְנֻת; from H2181 (זָנָה);
harlotry, i.e. (figuratively) idolatry
KJV: fornication, whoredom.

H8458.definition:
or תַּחְבּוּלָה; from H2254 (חָבַל) as denominative from H2256 (חֶבֶל);
(only in plural) properly, steerage (as a management of ropes), i.e. (figuratively) guidance or (by implication) a plan
KJV: good advice, (wise) counsels.

H8459.definition:
from an unused root meaning to depress; abasement;
Tochu, an Israelite
KJV: Tohu.

H8460.definition:
(Aramaic) or תּחֹת; (Aramaic), corresponding to H8478 (תַּחַת);
beneath
KJV: under.

H8461.definition:
probably for H2453 (חַכְמוֹנִי); sagacious;
Tachkemoni, an Israelite
KJV: Tachmonite.

H8462.definition:
from H2490 (חָלַל) in the sense of opening;
a commencement; rel. original (adverb, -ly)
KJV: begin(-ning), first (time).

H8463.definition:
or תַּחֲלֻא; from H2456 (חָלָא);
a malady
KJV: disease, [idiom] grievous, (that are) sick(-ness).

H8464.definition:
from H2554 (חָמַס);
a species of unclean bird (from its violence), perhaps an owl
KJV: night hawk.

H8465.definition:
probably from H2583 (חָנָה); station;
Tachan, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Tahan.

H8466.definition:
from H2583 (חָנָה);
(only plural collectively) an encampment
KJV: camp.

H8467.definition:
from H2603 (חָנַן);
graciousness; causatively, entreaty
KJV: favour, grace, supplication.

H8468.definition:
the same as H8467 (תְּחִנָּה);
Techinnah, an Israelite
KJV: Tehinnah.

H8469.definition:
or (feminine) תַּחֲנוּנָה; from H2603 (חָנַן);
earnest prayer
KJV: intreaty, supplication.

H8470.definition:
patronymically from H8465 (תַּחַן);
a Tachanite (collectively) or descendants of Tachan
KJV: Tahanites.

H8471.definition:
or תְּחַפְנְחֵס; (Ezekiel 30:18), or תַּחְפְּנֵס; (Jeremiah 2:16), of Egyptian derivation;
Tachpanches, Techaphneches or Tachpenes, a place in Egypt
KJV: Tahapanes, Tahpanhes, Tehaphnehes.

H8472.definition:
of Egyptian derivation;
Tachpenes, an Egyptian woman
KJV: Tahpenes.

H8473.definition:
from H2734 (חָרָה) in the original sense of H2352 (חוּר) or H2353 (חוּר);
a linen corslet (as white or hollow)
KJV: habergeon.

H8474.definition:
a facitious root from H2734 (חָרָה) through the idea of the heat of jealousy;
to vie with a rival
KJV: close, contend.

H8475.definition:
for H8390 (תַּאֲרֵעַ);
Tachrea, an Israelite
KJV: Tahrea.

H8476.definition:
probably of foreign derivation;
a (clean) animal with fur, probably a species of antelope
KJV: badger.

H8477.definition:
the same as H8476 (תַּחַשׁ);
Tachash, a relative of Abraham
KJV: Thahash.

H8478.definition:
from the same as H8430 (תּוֹחַ);
the bottom (as depressed); only adverbially, below (often with prepositional prefix underneath), in lieu of, etc.
KJV: as, beneath, [idiom] flat, in(-stead), (same) place (where...is), room, for...sake, stead of, under, [idiom] unto, [idiom] when...was mine, whereas, (where-) fore, with.

H8479.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H8478 (תַּחַת)
{the bottom (as depressed); only adverbially, below (often with prepositional prefix underneath), in lieu of, etc.}
KJV: under.

H8480.definition:
the same as H8478 (תַּחַת);
Tachath, the name of a place in the Desert, also of three Israelites
KJV: Tahath.

H8481.definition:
or תַּחְתֹּן; from H8478 (תַּחַת);
bottommost
KJV: lower(-est), nether(-most).

H8482.definition:
from H8478 (תַּחַת);
lowermost; as noun (feminine plural) the depths (figuratively, a pit, the womb)
KJV: low (parts, -er, -er parts, -est), nether (part).

H8483.definition:
apparently from the plural masculine of H8482 (תַּחְתִּי) or H8478 (תַּחַת) and H2320 (חֹדֶשׁ); lower (ones) monthly;
Tachtim-Chodshi, a place in Palestine
KJV: Tahtim-hodshi.

H8484.definition:
or תִּיכֹן; from H8432 (תָּוֶךְ);
central
KJV: middle(-most), midst.

H8485.definition:
or תֵּמָא; probably of foreign derivation;
Tema, a son of Ishmael, and the region settled by him
KJV: Tema.

H8486.definition:
or תֵּמָן; denominative from H3225 (יָמִין);
the south (as being on the right hand of a person facing the east)
KJV: south (side, -ward, wind).

H8487.definition:
or תֵּמָן; the same as H8486 (תֵּימָן);
Teman, the name of two Edomites, and of the region and descendant of one of them
KJV: south, Teman.

H8488.definition:
probably for H8489 (תֵּימָנִי);
Temeni, an Israelite
KJV: Temeni.

H8489.definition:
patronymically from H8487 (תֵּימָן);
a Temanite or descendant of Teman
KJV: Temani, Temanite.

H8490.definition:
or תִּמָרָה; from the same as H8558 (תָּמָר);
a column, i.e. cloud
KJV: pillar.

H8491.definition:
patrial or patronymically from an unused noun of uncertain meaning;
a Titsite or descendant or inhabitant of an unknown Tits
KJV: Tizite.

H8492.definition:
or תִּירֹשׁ; from H3423 (יָרַשׁ) in the sense of expulsion;
must or fresh grape-juice (as just squeezed out); by implication (rarely) fermented wine
KJV: (new, sweet) wine.

H8493.definition:
probably from H3372 (יָרֵא);
fearful, Tirja, an Israelite
KJV: Tiria.

H8494.definition:
probably of foreign derivation;
Tiras, a son of Japheth
KJV: Tiras.

H8495.definition:
from an unused root meaning to butt;
a buck or he-goat (as given to butting)
KJV: he goat.

H8496.definition:
or תּוֹך; (Psalm 72:14), from the same base as H8432 (תָּוֶךְ) (in the sense of cutting to pieces);
oppression
KJV: deceit, fraud.

H8497.definition:
a primitive root;
to strew, i.e. encamp
KJV: sit down.

H8498.definition:
feminine passive participle of H8505 (תָּכַן);
adjustment, i.e. structure; by implication, equipage
KJV: fashion, store.

H8499.definition:
from H3559 (כּוּן); or probably identical with H8498 (תְּכוּנָה);
something arranged or fixed, i.e. a place
KJV: seat.
